Subject: [PATCH] Fix installSplashScreen import path (still unresolved after
 prior fix)

installSplashScreen() is an extension function on Activity declared
inside SplashScreen's companion object, not a true top-level function.
The JVM/metalava view of it looks like a static method taking an
Activity parameter (which is why the Java call in MainActivity.java,
SplashScreen.installSplashScreen(this), works), but Kotlin resolves it
through extension-function rules and needs the class name kept in the
import path:

    import androidx.core.splashscreen.SplashScreen.installSplashScreen

Importing it as a bare androidx.core.splashscreen.installSplashScreen
(previous commit) treated it as fully top-level, which doesn't exist at
that path and left it unresolved - same error, same lines, in the next
CI run. The call site was already correct (bare installSplashScreen()).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
